{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["לא תאכלו על הדם — by its plain sense: a matter inferred from its context." "לא תנחשו ולא תעוננו — this too they would do according to the practices of the nations, who eat at the grave of a slain man for sorcery, so that he would not take vengeance, or other sorceries of that kind — similar to what we say concerning a nail from a crucifix. And our Sages interpreted it in several ways in tractate Sanhedrin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {1 "The final phrase, 'concerning a nail from a crucifix,' refers to a contemporary (12th-century northern French) folk-magical practice; rendered literally as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:07.661421527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}